<section class="lens-visual authority-visual" id="lens-authority-visual" aria-labelledby="authority-visual-title">
<header class="lens-visual-heading"><p class="lens-overline">Authority · illustrative record</p><h3 id="authority-visual-title">What an accepted definition looks like</h3><p>A definition supplies a precise meaning. Its acceptance record identifies who made that exact version authoritative and for which purpose.</p></header>
{{EXPORT_COMPLETENESS_DEFINITION}}
{{AUTHORITY_EXAMPLE}}
<p class="lens-principle"><strong>The general principle</strong> Accepted meaning gives a task its criterion. Permissions, required formats and permitted connections each have their own authority and scope.</p>
</section>

<section class="lens-visual provenance-visual" id="lens-provenance-visual" aria-labelledby="provenance-visual-title">
<header class="lens-visual-heading"><p class="lens-overline">Provenance · illustrative trace</p><h3 id="provenance-visual-title">Follow a claim back to what produced it</h3><p>A trace connects exact sources, the operation performed and its recorded result. Evidence relates those sources to a particular claim and its limits.</p></header>
{{PROVENANCE_EXAMPLE}}
<p class="lens-principle"><strong>The general principle</strong> Preserve the sources and transformations so someone else can inspect a conclusion. Evaluate how well they support that particular claim.</p>
<a class="lens-continue" href="#evidence">Continue to evidence and its limits →</a>
</section>

<section class="lens-visual lifecycle-visual" id="lens-lifecycle-visual" aria-labelledby="lifecycle-visual-title">
<header class="lens-visual-heading"><p class="lens-overline">Lifecycle · illustrative states</p><h3 id="lifecycle-visual-title">Different things can be in different states</h3><p>A lifecycle sets the states and permitted changes for a particular kind of item. Read each item’s state and change rules separately.</p></header>
{{LIFECYCLE_EXAMPLE}}
<p class="lens-principle"><strong>The general principle</strong> Record each item’s state and the authorized route for its next change. Acceptance, operation and information freshness have separate rules.</p>
<a class="lens-continue" href="#change">Continue to accepted changes and their effects →</a>
</section>
